the modern warfare 2 beta may have a  release window and it seems like your  starfield character won't be talking  much  call of duty modern warfare 2 is getting  a beta and according to an amazon  product page it could be coming in  august the page for modern warfare 2 on  playstation 5 says players who pre-order  will receive their beta code in august  the xbox series x and s page gets a  little more specific and says that those  who pre-order by august 15th will unlock  early access to the open beta now this  could suggest that the open beta will  start before then because once the early  access period ends anyone can jump in  however it's important to keep in mind  that activision has yet to announce any  dates but enough of activision let's  talk about its other half blizzard last  week diablo 4 game director joe shelley  revealed why the game doesn't have any  brand new classes according to shelley  the decision came down to player  expectations and making sure that the  aspects fans remember from previous  diablo games are present in diablo 4  albeit in a new modern form diablo  community lead adam fletcher recently  confirmed the plan is to eventually sell  paid expansions for d4 meaning it's  certainly possible that new classes  could be added to the game post-launch  but diablo 4 isn't coming until 2023 you  know what else isn't coming until then  starfield over on twitter bethesda  confirmed that you'll be a silent  protagonist in the new game this is  notable because fallout 4 the last  single player rpg from bethesda broke  new ground by having you play a voiced  character fallout 76 went back to the  silent trend though that was a large  multiplayer rpg the presentation at the  xbox and bethesda showcase made a point  to show how flexible the character  creator is in star field and like in  other bethesda rpgs you'll have loads of  dialogue options informed by your  characteristics and other choices but  you won't hear your created character  speak in 